<!--
  CNC.Common - shared non-wire infrastructure for the client/server split: the plumbing BOTH sides
  need but that carries no machine data and no wire shapes. ViewModelBase (INPC base every view
  model derives from), the UiContext/SyncTarget thread marshalling, and generic helpers.

  WHY IT EXISTS: client projects must drop their CNC Core reference (the contracts-only client
  discipline), but C# requires referencing the assembly that defines a used type's BASE class -
  so as long as ViewModelBase lived in CNC Core, no consumer of any view model could ever cut the
  reference. Sharing a LIBRARY is not the pass-C#-objects cheat; only machine-data instances
  crossing the client/server boundary are. Nothing in here may know about controllers, comms,
  g-code or wire messages - if a type needs any of those it belongs in CNC Core or CNC.Contracts.

  Types moved here from CNC Core keep their original namespace (CNC.Core) so the move needed zero
  call-site churn - same discipline as CNC.Contracts. This is the LEGACY net462 project the
  solution builds; CNC.Common.net8.csproj (same folder, same sources, NOT in the .sln) is the
  portability probe - the same two-project pattern as CNC Core and CNC Contracts.
-->
